    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Many random items, ideas, and experiences occur within the average lifetime. Often, these things are meaningless; however, sometimes they elicit varying public opinion.  In this podcast, we explore three \"items\" that polarize society: fruit, supplements, and clothing (or lack thereof). The narrative approach is a radio-play inspired by Dead Poet's Society. Listen with an open mind, and take time to ponder the question, \"What will YOU decide?\"",
